## Organ-node baseline VM args — REFERENCE TEMPLATE
##
## This template documents the canonical flag-set every organ-node spawn script
## inherits in W3 + downstream workstreams. Organ-nodes preserve the EPMD-isolation
## invariant (D8): no distributed-Erlang traffic between organ-nodes; all inter-organ
## traffic via Spine HTTP boundary.
##
## DO NOT execute this template directly. It is reference content consumed by W3+
## per-organ skeleton authoring + the harness BEAM node configuration.
##
## Per ea-m1-r1 §3 deliverable 2 + §4 verification 3 (empirical smoke test)
## EPMD-isolation invariant — Vigil-asserted via R5 CV scaffolding
## DOE 2026-06-02 / EA RFI-EA-2 ruling: substrate_l0_* sname pattern; organ-nodes use distinct namespace
##
## --------------------------------------------------------------------------
## CANONICAL ORGAN-NODE FLAG-SET
## --------------------------------------------------------------------------
##
## Empirical correction (DOE 2026-06-02 §4 verification step 3): the relay's
## "-no_epmd" framing was technically imprecise. `-no_epmd` is an erlexec-level
## flag that says "start distribution but without EPMD" and REQUIRES a paired
## `-proto_dist <Protocol>` arg specifying an alternative distribution transport.
## Organ-nodes that go through Spine HTTP have NO inter-organ distributed-Erlang
## need — distribution machinery should not start at all.
##
## Canonical mechanism: `-kernel start_distribution false`.
## This prevents distribution startup entirely → no EPMD registration → no
## distributed-Erlang traffic structurally possible. Node identifies as
## `nonode@nohost` regardless of any `-sname` provided.
##
## Canonical organ-node flag-set:

-sname <organ_slug>                  ## short-name for ps/diagnostics; distribution OFF below
-kernel start_distribution false      ## ENFORCE: no distribution, no EPMD registration
+K true                              ## kernel poll on (epoll/kqueue performance)
+A 32                                ## async thread pool

## Cookie posture: shared substrate-L0 cookie via ~/.erlang.cookie file-level inheritance.
## Cookie value is irrelevant under -kernel start_distribution false (no distribution attempts),
## but consistency-with-substrate-L0 is preserved by file-level sharing — no per-organ cookie variant.
##
## --------------------------------------------------------------------------
## EMPIRICAL VERIFICATION (2026-06-02 §4 step 3 — PASS)
## --------------------------------------------------------------------------
##
## Spawn pattern (b) verified empirically:
##   $ erl -sname test_canonical_organ -kernel start_distribution false \
##         -noinput -noshell -eval 'io:format("named-no-dist pid=~p node=~p~n", [self(), node()]), halt(0).'
##   named-no-dist pid=<0.10.0> node=nonode@nohost
##
##   $ epmd -names | grep test_canonical_organ
##   (no match — invariant holds)
##
## Pattern (a) — anonymous (no -sname at all) — also viable for short-lived worker procs;
## same empirical result: node identifies as nonode@nohost; no EPMD registration.
##
## Choice between (a) and (b): use (b) for long-lived organ-supervised procs (diagnostic
## visibility in `ps -axo args | grep beam.smp` worth the -sname); use (a) for short-lived
## escript-style workers spawned per-request.
